WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.369
-Jessica, thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:04.737
-Hi!

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:07.573
-And for doing the TikTok
Dance Challenge with me.

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:09.175
I'm happy
that you stayed with me

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.177
and that we're still friends
even past that.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.279
-[ Laughs ]
-It was very embarrassing.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:17.182
You were my guest on the show
early in the quarantine,

00:00:17.182 --> 00:00:20.886
and, gosh,
we're now six months in.

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:23.089
I appreciate you doing the show.
How is everyone doing?

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.891
How's the fam?

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:27.360
-We are hanging in there.
-Good.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.496
-We just started school.
-Oh, boy.

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:33.432
-Which is the opposite of fun.

00:00:33.432 --> 00:00:37.904
Even just getting the kids
to bed is like --

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.238
I'm like, "Why are we having

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:41.574
a discussion
at 9:00 p.m., Haven?

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.109
You're 9 years old.
-9?

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.011
-You should be
going to bed at 7:00."

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:46.145
Yeah.
-Wait.

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:48.848
I heard that you guys took
a family RV trip,

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.717
and I want to know about this.
-We did.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:54.954
I booked two trips,
meaning that we found houses

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:59.959
that are in two different states
and that were near water

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:03.462
so that we can do activities,
right?

00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:04.964
-Great idea.
-And I've never really seen

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:08.368
the great outdoors.
I'm not really that person.

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:11.738
-No, me neither, but I feel like
I am somewhere in my soul.

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:14.374
-Somewhere in my soul,
I felt like maybe

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:19.879
I was more in tune
or I'd find myself in nature.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.915
No, I didn't.
Nope.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:24.117
Opposite of that one.
-Really?

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:28.554
-And, you know, I just feel like
some people should never

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:34.760
spend long periods of time
in cars or RVs or vans,

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.396
and that would be
my entire family.

00:01:37.396 --> 00:01:41.300
-No one liked it?
-No -- The thing is, like,

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.435
it's just not natural, I guess,

00:01:43.435 --> 00:01:45.905
for my children
to be in anything that moves,

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:48.107
'cause they immediately
start throwing up.

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:51.010
-[ Laughing ]
-Like, immediately.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:55.281
So we stop in Zion,
and Hayes --

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:56.482
and I'm like, "Oh, my gosh.

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:58.951
We haven't had a kid barf
in like six hours,"

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:01.888
so I'm like, "Victory!"
-That's the goal.

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:03.856
-But then,
right when we stopped,

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:07.093
Hayes was like, "Mommy, uppy."
He says, "I'm full."

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:09.028
He was like,
"Uppy, uppy! I'm full!

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:12.098
So, I take him out of
the car-seat thingy,

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:17.570
and he booted
all over my fa--

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.339
In my mouth, in my eyeballs.

00:02:20.339 --> 00:02:24.043
And everyone in the car -- in
the van was like "Ew!"

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:27.580
So they bolt out...
-The weird part is that --

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:31.450
The weirdest part
is that he's 15.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:34.186
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:34.186 --> 00:02:36.355
Come on, come on.
Can't we make jokes?

00:02:36.355 --> 00:02:39.159
-You do, you do!
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:42.628
-So, kids are barfing,
and I'm, like,

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:45.798
trying to make
the situation good.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.800
I'm like,
"Once we get to this --"

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:50.970
I was like, "I planned this trip
where we're gonna go see --"

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:54.607
It's an organic,
sustainable farm, right?

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:57.976
-Ah.
-But then...

00:02:57.976 --> 00:03:00.179
First of all, the stench.

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:02.581
So, all my kids
have the smell of, like --

00:03:02.581 --> 00:03:04.717
-This sounds like a nightmare.

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:07.320
-The smell and all the things.
-It's a farm.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.922
-And then we go
to the chicken coop.

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:12.425
It's 112 degrees.
Right?

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:16.529
And my friend is so lovely.
And, literally, this is one of

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.998
the best, well-run,
most sustainable,

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.000
humane farms there are.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.636
And then,
you open the coop thing,

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:27.406
and we saw an egg plop out...
-Nature.

00:03:27.406 --> 00:03:30.944
-...and his eyes bugging out
of his head.

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:34.747
And did you know
there's like a slime...

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:36.982
-No, no.
No, no, there's not.

00:03:36.982 --> 00:03:38.484
-There's like a bit
that comes out with it.

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:41.220
-No, no, there's not a thing.
-Yes, there's a bit.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:44.157
-No, no, no, no.
Don't ruin -- Don't ruin eggs.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:46.759
-He was like -- [ Gasps ]
-I'm like that, too.

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:49.595
I'm like, "What?"
Pal, I want to talk to you

00:03:49.595 --> 00:03:51.030
about "L.A.'s Finest."

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.532
Season 2
is available on Spectrum.

00:03:53.532 --> 00:03:54.767
And season 1 --
this is a big deal --

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.802
is gonna premiere on Fox.
-Yes.

00:03:56.802 --> 00:04:00.139
-Literally national TV.
-So, it's basically,

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:04.177
take the "Bad Boys" universe,
with Martin Lawrence

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:05.445
and Will Smith...
-Yep.

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:08.547
-...and instead, you have me
and Gabrielle Union

00:04:08.547 --> 00:04:13.653
and Gab's character from
"Bad Boys," coming into L.A.,

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:16.989
and we partner up,
and you just get to see

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:21.694
two women kicking butt,
having fun, cracking jokes.

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:23.930
And then, there's
lots of cool mystery

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:27.533
as we're really discovering
about each other's past.

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:30.603
-I can't think of two
more perfect combo

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:32.672
of you and Gabrielle Union,
because, gosh,

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:35.708
is she funny, as well.
-She is.

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:37.910
-You guys also produce the show.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:41.580
What is the best part of
producing a show like this?

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.783
-I think what's so cool
about producing this show

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:47.453
is that you don't get to see
a lot of black and brown people

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:51.957
in positions of leadership
in Hollywood at all, right?

00:04:51.957 --> 00:04:54.360
Behind the camera
or in front of the camera.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.962
So, we're the leads
of a show, right?

00:04:56.962 --> 00:05:01.533
So that in itself
is pretty rare for Hollywood.

00:05:01.533 --> 00:05:05.237
And then, being leads of a show
in the action genre

00:05:05.237 --> 00:05:09.042
and being women, again,
it's totally unprecedented,

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:11.544
and people just don't do it.

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:13.912
And then, also,
behind the camera, you know,

00:05:13.912 --> 00:05:16.715
showrunners to
head of the writers' room,

00:05:16.715 --> 00:05:20.085
and we kind of just prove
that you can have diversity

00:05:20.085 --> 00:05:23.890
and inclusion behind the camera,
in front of the camera.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:27.460
You can also write a show
that is inclusive

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:30.396
and represents diversity
in a way that doesn't

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:33.132
feed into a stereotype
or a stigma,

00:05:33.132 --> 00:05:35.101
and you can be successful at it.
-Yeah.

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:37.303
-And it's still fun, and it's
great to watch for everyone.

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:40.239
You make a great show.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:42.675
Here are Jessica Alba
and Gabrielle Union

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:45.144
in "L.A.'s Finest."
Take a look.

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:47.180
-You, sir?
Drinks?

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:55.087
Private security, armed.
Front door, hallway.

00:05:55.087 --> 00:05:58.024
-Okay?
-We need a distraction.

00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:00.326
-Me? No.
That's your job.

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:02.362
-No.
-Hey, cocktails.

00:06:06.598 --> 00:06:08.768
Mr. Jefferies wants you.

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:12.471
His friend likes to slum it
with the help.

00:06:12.471 --> 00:06:17.075
-I thought I was just supposed
to serve drinks here.

00:06:17.075 --> 00:06:19.112
-You've been promoted.

00:06:21.414 --> 00:06:22.881
-Slum it.
-Slummin' it.

00:06:22.881 --> 00:06:24.016
-I know.
That was excessive.

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:25.551
-I mean...
-As if.

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:27.620
-These guys would be lucky
to have some of this.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:28.821
-All of that.

00:06:28.821 --> 00:06:30.656
-Jessica, thank you so much
for being here.

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:33.325
Season two of "L.A.'s Finest"
is available now

00:06:33.325 --> 00:06:35.460
to Spectrum Video subscribers,

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:37.863
and season 1 will have
its network broadcast premiere

00:06:37.863 --> 00:06:40.400
this Monday,
at 8:00 p.m., on Fox.

